 towers and clearing obstacles.","Compare the playable towers, waves, and building space with the original author prompt.","Download this game’s archive and trace one mechanic from input through game state to feedback.","Use the framework quick start for a new attempt, then compare the result against the same brief. Generation requires your own provider access.","The authors present this as a single-prompt OpenGame result. Use the published brief and generated project to study how an agent connects game rules, assets, and interaction.",[482,483,484,485],{"_53":480,"_28":257,"_20":278},{"_53":476,"_28":460,"_20":269,"_258":477},{"_53":471,"_28":472,"_258":473,"_309":310},{"_53":256,"_28":257,"_258":468},[117,307,308],"resource:opengame","resource","Generates browser game projects with reusable templates and debugging skills.","/resources/",{"_22":117,"_565":95,"_297":113,"_51":566,"_564":495,"_559":558,"_28":520,"_61":567,"_545":568,"_538":569,"_534":570,"_530":571,"_527":226},[500,501,502,503,504,505,506,507,508,509,510,511,512,513,514],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_51":24,"_55":95,"_57":565,"_59":-7},{"_51":111,"_55":495,"_57":564,"_59":-7},{"_51":52,"_53":562,"_55":563,"_57":297,"_59":90},{"_51":52,"_53":560,"_55":561,"_57":51,"_59":90},{"_51":52,"_53":557,"_55":558,"_57":559,"_59":60},{"_51":61,"_53":262,"_63":555,"_57":28,"_59":-7},{"_51":61,"_53":550,"_63":551,"_57":61,"_59":-7},{"_51":237,"_53":543,"_285":532,"_63":544,"_57":545,"_59":-7},{"_51":237,"_53":536,"_285":532,"_63":537,"_57":538,"_59":-7},{"_51":237,"_53":531,"_285":532,"_63":533,"_57":534,"_59":-7},{"_51":52,"_53":528,"_55":529,"_57":530,"_59":90},{"_51":52,"_53":526,"_55":226,"_57":527,"_59":90},{"_51":227,"_57":524,"_53":525,"_74":76,"_82":81,"_35":257,"_58":56},{"_51":52,"_57":521,"_53":522,"_55":523},{"_51":61,"_57":515,"_53":516,"_63":517},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[518],{"_53":519,"_28":520},"The Chinese University of Hong Kong · MMLab","https://github.com/leigest519/OpenGame","identity","Identity & attribution","The official README directly identifies the author team as CUHK MMLab and lists CUHK email addresses. Uses the university's official website icon to identify that affiliation.","projectMedia","Creator project media","Source reviewed","verified","Year","2026","year","Tracks",false,[88,535],"dimensions","3D","Development stages",[539,540,541,542],"stages","Planning","Gameplay & code","Assets & animation","Testing","Topics",[546,547,548,549],"tags","Browser games","Game Skill","Browser feedback","GameCoder-27B","Further reading",[552],{"_53":553,"_28":554},"Paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18394",[556],{"_53":262,"_28":520},"Why it belongs here","Turns natural-language requirements into web projects using Template Skill and Debug Skill for Canvas, Phaser, three.js, and other templates. The public CLI accepts OpenAI-compatible model endpoints; the paper also introduces GameCoder-27B. Browser execution and visual judging assess build health, usability, and intent alignment. The README still lists the standalone evaluation pipeline as forthcoming; model weights and full evaluation reproducibility are not established by the framework release alone.","detail","Resource type","Agent","Category","2D development","summary","name","agent",[577],[546,547,548,549],[573,574,575,576],[113,572],2026,"3d","plan","code","assets","test",{"_53":553,"_28":554},{"_579":580},"documents",{"_581":582,"_583":584},"en",[586,590,591,592,589,593,594,595,596,597,598,599,600,601,602,603,604,605,606,607,608,609,610,611,612,613,614,615,616,617,618,619,620,621,622,623,624,588,625,587,626,627,628,629,630,631,632,633,634,635,636,637,638,639,640,641,642,643],"zh",[585,586,587,588,589],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-rese